  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n{x⁴} + ( {(1)/({{x⁴)}}} ) = 322\n\n**Formula used:**\n\n(a+b)²=a²+b²+2ab\n\na³-b³=(a-b)(a²+b²+ab)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nUsing a³-b³=(a-b)(a²+b²+ab),\n\n{x³} - ( {(1)/({{x³)}}} )=( {x-(1)/({{x)}}} )( {x²+(1)/({{x²)}}} +1 ) ....(1)\n\nNow, using (a+b)²=a²+b²+2ab,\n\n{x⁴} + ( {(1)/({{x⁴)}}} ) = ( { x²+(1)/({{x²)}}} )² -2=322\n\n∴ ( { x²+(1)/({{x²)}}} )² =324\n\n∴ ( { x²+(1)/({{x²)}}} )=18 .... (2)\n\nAgain, using (a+b)²=a²+b²+2ab,\n\n{x²} + ( {(1)/({{x²)}}} ) = ( { x-(1)/({{x)}}} )² +2=18\n\n∴ ( { x-(1)/({{x)}}} )² =16\n\n∴ ( { x-(1)/({{x)}}} )=4 ....(3)\n\nSubstituting (2), (3) in (1),\n\n{x³} - ( {(1)/({{x³)}}} )=4 times (18+1) = 76\n\n**∴ If {x⁴} + ( {(1)/({{x⁴)}}} ) = 322, then what is the value of {x³} - ( {(1)/({{x³)}}} )= ****76**.",
